module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphism.TwistEventual
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.CanonicalSymSurjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.DegreeOne
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Stacks Tag 07ZR: the twist on the relative `Proj` of an algebra generated in degree one

Let `S` be a scheme and let `A` be a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `A_1` over
`A_0`. Write `X = Proj_S(A)`. Stacks Tag 07ZR asserts that `𝒪_X(1)` is invertible and very ample
relative to `X ⟶ S`: the morphism attached to the canonical graded-algebra map `Sym(A_1) ⟶ A` is
a closed immersion `X ⟶ 𝐏(A_1)` over `S` which pulls `𝒪_{𝐏(A_1)}(1)` back to `𝒪_X(1)`.

`𝒪_X(1)` is the degree-one piece `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag07ZGTwist.relativeTwist A 1` of the
glued twist algebra of Stacks Tag 01NR, which exists for every quasi-coherent graded algebra.
Its invertibility is Stacks Tag 01O4 in a single degree: over each affine open of the base it is
the absolute twist `𝒪(1)` of `Proj Γ(U, A)`, and generation in degree one trivializes that twist
near every point.

The canonical map `Sym(A_1) ⟶ A` is `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymHom`; it is
surjective on homogeneous sections over every affine open of the base in every positive degree,
so by Stacks Tag 07ZK (1) and (2) its morphism `r_ψ` of Stacks Tag 07ZG is defined on all of `X`
and is a closed immersion, `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom`. By Stacks Tag
07ZK (3) the maps `θ_n : r_ψ^* 𝒪_{𝐏(A_1)}(n) ⟶ 𝒪_X(n)` are isomorphisms, the source `Sym(A_1)`
being generated in degree one; in degree one that is the identification of `𝒪_X(1)` with the
pullback of `𝒪_{𝐏(A_1)}(1)`, and with the closed immersion it is relative very ampleness in the
sense of Stacks Tag 01VM.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.twistOne`: **`𝒪_X(1)` on the relative `Proj` of a graded algebra.**
* `Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.twistOneIsoPullback`: **the closed immersion `X ⟶ 𝐏(A_1)` pulls
  `𝒪_{𝐏(A_1)}(1)` back to `𝒪_X(1)`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag07ZGTwist.isIso_relativeTwistMap_of_affineSections`: Stacks Tag
  07ZK (3) under surjectivity on the sections over the affine opens of the base.
* `Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.isInvertibleModule_twistOne`: **`𝒪_X(1)` is invertible.**
* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.isClosedImmersion_canonicalSymProjHom` (in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.CanonicalSymSurjective`): **the morphism
  `X ⟶ 𝐏(A_1)` is a closed immersion.**
* `Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.isRelativelyVeryAmple_twistOne`: **`𝒪_X(1)` is very ample relative to
  `X ⟶ S`**, in the sense of `Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple`, Stacks Tag 01VM.

## Implementation notes

**Surjectivity on affine sections rather than epimorphy.** Stacks Tag 07ZK asks that
`A_d → B_d` be surjective for `d ≫ 0`. What is used of this for a map out of a quasi-coherent
algebra is the surjectivity on the sections over each affine open of the base, which is what
`Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom` provides
for the canonical map; the third assertion of Tag 07ZK is restated here over that hypothesis, as
its first two are in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.CanonicalSymSurjective`.

**Invertibility is not an instance.** Generation in degree one is an explicit hypothesis of
`Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.isInvertibleModule_twistOne`, so the invertibility needed to state
relative very ampleness is supplied by `have` in the statement, as the definition of
`Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple` does for quasi-coherence of `E`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Filter
open Stacks.Ample
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain
open Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple

universe u

/-! ### Tag 07ZK (3) over surjectivity on affine sections -/

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag07ZGTwist

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A B : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S} (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B)

/-- **Stacks Tag 07ZK (3)** over the surjectivity hypothesis: if `ψ : A ⟶ B` is surjective on
homogeneous sections over every affine open of the base in all sufficiently large degrees and `A`
is generated by `A_1` over `A_0`, then for every `n` the map
`θ_n : r_ψ^* 𝒪_{Proj_S(A)}(n) ⟶ 𝒪_{Proj_S(B)}(n)|_{U(ψ)}` of Stacks Tag 07ZG is an isomorphism.

Over every affine open of the base this is the third assertion of Stacks Tag 01N1 for the induced
homomorphism of graded rings of sections. -/
theorem isIso_relativeTwistMap_of_affineSections (hψ : EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections ψ)
    (hgen : ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso (relativeTwistMap ψ n) :=
  isIso_relativeTwistMap_of_forall_chart ψ n fun U => by
    have h := ProjTwistMono.isIso_projMapData_twistMap _ _ (ψ.sectionHom U.1)
      (eventually_surjective_gradedAddHom_of_affineSections ψ hψ U.2) (hgen U.1 U.2) n
    rwa [ProjTwistCompare.projMapData_twistMap] at h

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag07ZGTwist

namespace Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple

variable {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### The twist `𝒪_X(1)` -/

/-- **The twist `𝒪_X(1)` on `X = Proj_S(A)`**, for a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `A`:
the degree-one piece of the glued twist algebra of Stacks Tag 01NR. -/
abbrev twistOne (A : SheafGradedAlgebra S) : (relativeProj A).scheme.Modules :=
  Tag07ZGTwist.relativeTwist A 1

/-- **The chart identification of `𝒪_X(1)`**: over every affine open `U` of the base it restricts
along the chart to the absolute twist `𝒪(1)` of `Proj Γ(U, A)`. -/
def twistOneChartIso (A : SheafGradedAlgebra S) (U : S.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Scheme.Modules.restrict (twistOne A) ((relativeProj A).chart U hU) ≅
      AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (A.grading U) 1 :=
  Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.gluedChartIso A 1 (ProjTwistCocycle.isNestedCocycle A 1) U hU

/-- **Stacks Tag 07ZR: `𝒪_X(1)` is an invertible `𝒪_X`-module**, for `X = Proj_S(A)` the relative
homogeneous spectrum of a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `A_1` over `A_0`.

This is Stacks Tag 01O4 in a single degree: `𝒪_X(1)` is the absolute twist `𝒪(1)` on each affine
chart of `X`, and the graded ring of sections over each affine open of the base is generated by
its degree-one part, which trivializes that twist near every point. -/
@[stacks 07ZR "O_X(1) is invertible"]
theorem isInvertibleModule_twistOne (A : SheafGradedAlgebra S)
    (hgen : ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A) :
    IsInvertibleModule (relativeProj A).scheme (twistOne A) :=
  Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.isInvertibleModule_of_chartIso (twistOne A) 1 (twistOneChartIso A) hgen

/-! ### The closed immersion into `𝐏(A_1)` pulls `𝒪(1)` back to `𝒪_X(1)` -/

variable (A : SheafGradedAlgebra S) (hgen : ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A)

include hgen in
/-- The map `θ_n` of Stacks Tag 07ZG for the canonical map `Sym(A_1) ⟶ A` is an isomorphism: Stacks
Tag 07ZK (3), the source `Sym(A_1)` being generated in degree one. -/
theorem isIso_relativeTwistMap_canonicalSymHom (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso (Tag07ZGTwist.relativeTwistMap (canonicalSymHom A) n) :=
  Tag07ZGTwist.isIso_relativeTwistMap_of_affineSections _
    (eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom A hgen)
    (Stacks.SymGraded.isGeneratedInDegreeOne_schemeSheafGradedAlgebra _ _) n

/-- **Stacks Tag 07ZR: the closed immersion `X ⟶ 𝐏(A_1)` pulls `𝒪_{𝐏(A_1)}(1)` back to
`𝒪_X(1)`.** The closed immersion is `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom`, the
morphism of Stacks Tag 07ZG attached to the canonical map `Sym(A_1) ⟶ A` read on all of `X`, and
the isomorphism is the inverse of the map `θ_1` of Tag 07ZG, which is an isomorphism by Stacks
Tag 07ZK (3). -/
@[stacks 07ZR "the closed immersion X -> P(A_1) pulls back O_{P(A_1)}(1) to O_X(1)"]
def twistOneIsoPullback :
    twistOne A ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback (canonicalSymProjHom A hgen)).obj
        (Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.twistOne (A.piece 1)) :=
  haveI := isIso_relativeTwistMap_canonicalSymHom A hgen 1
  ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackId _).app (twistOne A)).symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr (topDomainIso_hom_ι (canonicalSymHom A) _)).symm.app
      (twistOne A) ≪≫
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp _ (canonicalSymHom A).relativeMapDomain.ι).app
      (twistOne A)).symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback _).mapIso
      (asIso (Tag07ZGTwist.relativeTwistMap (canonicalSymHom A) 1)).symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp
        (topDomainIso (canonicalSymHom A) (relativeMapDomain_eq_top_of_affineSections _
          (eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom A hgen))).hom
        (Tag07ZGMorphism.relativeMapHom (canonicalSymHom A))).app
      (Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.twistOne (A.piece 1))

include hgen in
/-- **Stacks Tag 07ZR: `𝒪_X(1)` is very ample relative to `X ⟶ S`**, for `X = Proj_S(A)` the
relative homogeneous spectrum of a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `A_1` over
`A_0`.

Relative very ampleness is Stacks Tag 01VM,
`Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple`: the quasi-coherent module on the base is `A_1`,
the immersion over the base is the closed immersion
`Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom` attached to the canonical map
`Sym(A_1) ⟶ A`, and the identification of `𝒪_X(1)` with its pullback of `𝒪_{𝐏(A_1)}(1)` is
`Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.twistOneIsoPullback`. -/
@[stacks 07ZR "O_X(1) is relatively very ample on X/S", ega "II 4.4.3" "Case X = Proj_Y(S)"]
theorem isRelativelyVeryAmple_twistOne :
    have := isInvertibleModule_twistOne A hgen
    Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple (relativeProj A).toBase (twistOne A) :=
  haveI := isInvertibleModule_twistOne A hgen
  haveI := isClosedImmersion_canonicalSymProjHom A hgen
  Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.isRelativelyVeryAmple_of_immersion _ _ (A.piece 1)
    (canonicalSymProjHom A hgen) inferInstance (canonicalSymProjHom_comp_toBase A hgen)
    (twistOneIsoPullback A hgen)

end Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple

end
